{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/977447-combined-attainment-house-rule","id":977447,"title":"Combined Attainment house-rule.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-27T16:03:17-07:00","id":977447,"title":"Combined Attainment house-rule.","content":"So I've read around that there is an implication of being able to have an Attainment of two spells, and not just one. So I decided to put together the mechanics for it. Specifically, for two forms of it, whichever is better. <br /> <br /> Form 1: From the 3rd Attainment above, you can instead have the ability be 2 different spell combined together. Reach is calculated by the higher of the two spells, so a combined effect of a 2 dot and 3 dot spell in the 3rd Attainment slot will only have 1 Reach for each effect to be allocated. The combined effects share the same casting speed and duration should Reach be allocated accordingly. <br /> <br /> Form 2: Same as before, only the total Reach is calculated as if it were one spell. So in the previous example, instead of 2 total Reach, 1 for each effect, you would have 1 Reach all around, for both effects. <br /> <br /> I made this up about 2 weeks ago statting up my take on the Sphinxes, but never considered sharing it till now. Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T16:44:47-07:00","id":977470,"title":"","content":"It should work like combined spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":"